{
  "requirement": "`Comment` covers source comments, including documentation comments.\n`Annotation` covers language constructs such as attributes and decorators\nthat annotate a declaration. Providers use the common kind when it applies\nand `Other` with a language-defined name for additional kinds.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub enum AttachmentKind {\n    Comment,\n    Annotation,\n    Other(String),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for AttachmentKind;\nimpl Debug for AttachmentKind;\nimpl PartialEq for AttachmentKind;\nimpl Eq for AttachmentKind;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations from `requirements.sdk.outlines.AttachmentKind` and the tests that cover them:\n\n- **`Comment` covers source comments, including doc comments.**\n  - `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[rust_attachments_keep_the_owner_kind_and_original_bytes]` asserts `Comment` for `//!`, `///` and trailing `//` comments.\n  - `bundled_languages_classify_only_their_attachment_syntax` asserts `Comment` for Rust block doc comments (`/*!`, `/**`, `/*`), Python and TOML/YAML `#` comments, TS/TSX comments, CSS comments and Markdown HTML comments.\n  - The same test asserts that string and literal lookalikes are not classified, and that plain text has no attachments.\n- **`Annotation` covers attributes and decorators.** `#[inline]`, Python `@a` and `@pkg.decorate(...)`, and TS/TSX `@dec` are asserted as `Annotation`.\n- **`Other` with a language-defined name for additional kinds.** `custom_attachment_spans_are_checked_against_the_original_snapshot` has a custom provider emit `AttachmentKind::Other(\"marker\".into())`. It asserts the kind round-trips with the payload through `assert_eq!`.\n- **Providers use the common kind when it applies.** The bundled-language tests assert that the common kinds are used for each language's comment and annotation syntax.\n- **`Clone`, `Debug` and `PartialEq`.** The tests call `.kind.clone()` and use `assert_eq!` on kinds, and `assert_eq!` needs `Debug` and `PartialEq`. `recovered_outlines_keep_the_diagnostic_and_intact_items` and `outline_constructors_preserve_fields_and_replace_attachments` also compare kinds with `==` and `assert_eq!`.\n- **The enum shape (`#[non_exhaustive]`, the three variants) and the trait implementations including `Eq`.** No dedicated `AttachmentKind` test checks `Eq`. `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` compares rustdoc's generated declaration and trait-implementation list for each exported item against the specification, so this check should cover the missing `Eq` assertion. I read `RustdocSignatures::declaration` and `trait_impls` through search snippets, not in full. I did not confirm that `AttachmentKind` is among the compared items.\n\nNo unacknowledged gap found.",
  "references": "a0eb425b7335bdba3162ac71ca4bac1d2b4dea507b6f6bb4c82bdc79e416b394",
